"comparison": "Both Citigroup and Bank of America identify the FDIC special assessment as a key driver of noninterest expense variance between 2023 and 2024, but the nature of the impact differs. Citigroup reports that excluding FDIC special assessments (and divestitures) expenses decreased 2%, implying the assessment was a headwind or normalization factor against which underlying efficiency was measured. In contrast, Bank of America highlights that its 2024 expense decrease of $2.4 billion was primarily due to the 'absence of a $2.1 billion prior-year accrual' for the FDIC special assessment recorded in 2023. While C's metric isolates the 2024 assessment impact alongside divestitures, BAC's variance is structurally driven by the one-time 2023 charge no longer being present in 2024.",
